      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Camp_Dennison"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The camp served as a recruiting, training, and medical post for Union soldiers during the Civil War.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Camp_Dennison"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Little Miami Railroad ran through the camp, allowing rapid troop movement to Cincinnati.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Camp_Dennison"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Soldiers lived in wooden barracks that were later turned into hospital wards.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Camp_Dennison"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "After the camp closed, many nearby homes were built from its abandoned lumber.",
